---
import DemoShell from '../DemoShell.astro';
import Control from './Control.astro';
---

<DemoShell
  id="demo-impedance"
  code="D4"
  title="Impedance — Nyquist, Bode, DRT"
  poster="d4-impedance.svg"
  alt="Nyquist plot with two semicircles and a Warburg tail, Bode magnitude and phase plots, and the distribution of relaxation times showing separated peaks"
  aspect="16/10"
  stack={true}
  caption="An equivalent-circuit spectrum from 10 mHz to 100 kHz, and its distribution of relaxation times γ(τ), inverted live. Hover the DRT to mark the matching frequency on the Nyquist curve."
  presets={[
    { label: 'Aged cell: a second arc grows in', state: { 'd4-age': 200 } },
    { label: 'Noisy data, λ too small: false spikes', state: { 'd4-noise': 2, 'd4-lambda': 0.0001 } },
    { label: 'λ too large: two processes merge into one', state: { 'd4-age': 200, 'd4-noise': 0, 'd4-lambda': 1 } },
  ]}
>
  <fieldset class="panel" slot="panel" disabled>
    <legend>equivalent circuit · frequency response analyser</legend>
    <div class="control-cols">
      <Control id="d4-rohm" label="R_Ω / Ω cm²" min={0} max={50} value={10} step={0.1} />
      <Control id="d4-rct" label="R_ct / Ω cm²" min={1} max={100} value={25} scale="log" />
      <Control id="d4-cdl" label="C_dl / F cm⁻²" min={1e-6} max={1e-3} value={2e-5} scale="log" />
      <Control id="d4-rd" label="R_d / Ω cm²" min={0} max={100} value={30} step={0.5} />
      <Control id="d4-taud" label="τ_d = L²/D / s" min={0.01} max={100} value={2} scale="log" />
      {/* SEI age stays slider-only: its readout is a state name, not a quantity. */}
      <div class="control-row">
        <label for="d4-age">SEI age</label>
        <input type="range" id="d4-age" min="0" max="300" step="5" value="0" />
        <output class="readout" id="d4-age-out" for="d4-age">fresh</output>
      </div>
      <Control id="d4-noise" label="noise / % of |Z|" min={0} max={5} value={0} step={0.1} />
      <Control id="d4-lambda" label="DRT λ (Tikhonov)" min={1e-4} max={1} value={1e-2} scale="log" />
    </div>
    <div class="switch-row">
      <button class="tool-btn" type="button" id="d4-analyse">open this spectrum in the analyser →</button>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-readouts">
      <span>DRT misfit <output id="d4-misfit">—</output></span>
      <span>Σ R from DRT <output id="d4-rsum">—</output></span>
      <span>cursor <output id="d4-hover">—</output></span>
    </div>
  </fieldset>
  <Fragment slot="notes">
    <p>
      The circuit is R<sub>Ω</sub> + [R<sub>SEI</sub> ∥ C<sub>SEI</sub>] + [C<sub>dl</sub> ∥
      (R<sub>ct</sub> + Z<sub>W</sub>)] with a finite-length Warburg. The DRT is recovered by
      Tikhonov-regularised non-negative least squares on about 60 log-spaced relaxation times.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        γ is a density in ln τ: the <em>area</em> under a peak is the resistance of that process.
        Peak height depends on the grid and should not be read as a quantity.
      </li>
      <li>
        The Warburg tail has no single relaxation time, so it appears as a broad band of τ. That is
        expected, not an artefact.
      </li>
      <li>
        The noise control adds seeded Gaussian error proportional to |Z|. With clean data almost any
        λ looks fine; it takes noise to see why the choice matters.
      </li>
      <li>The Nyquist panel keeps equal axis scaling, so a semicircle is a semicircle.</li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</DemoShell>

<style is:global>
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    #demo-impedance .demo-stage {
      aspect-ratio: 9/16 !important;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { initWhenVisible } from './runtime';
  initWhenVisible('demo-impedance', async (shell) => {
    const { init } = await import('./d4-eis');
    init(shell);
  });
</script>
